+## Printout definitions and pure validation
+
+`GET /printout-types` returns only PLANNED and AVAILABLE rows in the normal success envelope. Every item has `{id,code,name,category,description,scope,status,endpoint,icon,definitionVersion,supportedFormats,optionsSchema,optionsUi,initialValues}`. `endpoint` is null until an actual generator is registered; `icon` is a semantic frontend registry key. There is no `canGenerate` property. `requiredOptions` is a database-only, code-owned projection and is omitted from the response.
+
+For a defined report, `definitionVersion` is a positive integer, `supportedFormats` is an array of `pdf|docx|xlsx`, `optionsSchema` is JSON Schema 2020-12, `optionsUi` is `{sections:[{id,label,fields:[{path,control,suffix?}]}]}`, and `initialValues` is an object. Fields use JSON Pointer paths. The control allowlist is `text|textarea|number|select|multiSelect|selectButton|checkbox|switch|date`; metadata contains no executable code, HTML, selectors or CSS. Unsupported definitions fail the consistency gate before exposure. Initial values can intentionally omit required properties; schema defaults are never inserted, types never coerced, and extra option properties never removed silently.
+
