+
+Choice controls use closed nonempty `oneOf` entries with primitive `const` values, or `enum` values, matching scalar `type` (`string`, `number`, `integer`). Array selection controls use the same contract on `items`; no object/boolean choices or implicit string conversion. Numeric zero remains a number. Array uniqueness is enforced when declared by the schema. The semantic date control requires `{type:"string",format:"date"}`. Both validators register the same strict calendar-date format: exactly `YYYY-MM-DD` and a valid Luxon ISO date that round-trips unchanged; timestamps and impossible dates are rejected. This uses existing Luxon with no additional format dependency.
+
